WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:18.630
Lemonade Detectives watched as Robby stomped away without another word.

2
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.511
"What's wrong with him?"

3
00:00:20.791 --> 00:00:22.973
Cole asked, still staring after Robby.

4
00:00:23.853 --> 00:00:25.634
Henry was wondering the same thing.

5
00:00:26.395 --> 00:00:28.176
Robby's behavior seemed suspicious.

6
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.801
"Why is Robby so mad at Mr.

7
00:00:31.881 --> 00:00:33.862
Tate?" he asked one of the other kids.

8
00:00:33.882 --> 00:00:36.783
"I don't know," the kid said.

9
00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:39.845
"Anyway, I think I hear my mom calling me."

10
00:00:40.645 --> 00:00:41.305
He ran off.

11
00:00:42.306 --> 00:00:43.526
Henry looked at another kid.

12
00:00:43.546 --> 00:00:46.087
"Why's everybody acting so weird?"

13
00:00:46.347 --> 00:00:47.008
he asked him.

14
00:00:47.028 --> 00:00:49.549
"Is it because of what Robby said?"

15
00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:51.930
"No. Maybe.

16
00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:53.811
I mean, I have to go too."

17
00:00:54.591 --> 00:00:56.832
The second kid scooped up the ball and hurried away.

18
00:00:58.536 --> 00:01:01.298
Two others left after him, leaving only Emma.

19
00:01:01.318 --> 00:01:03.159
"What's going on?"

20
00:01:03.519 --> 00:01:04.439
Maggie asked Emma.

21
00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:07.241
"Why did Robby get so angry just now?

22
00:01:08.061 --> 00:01:09.122
Does he really want Mr.

23
00:01:09.182 --> 00:01:10.763
Tate to leave West Belltown?"

24
00:01:10.783 --> 00:01:14.725
"I guess," Emma said in a soft voice.

25
00:01:14.745 --> 00:01:16.646
"But why?"

26
00:01:16.946 --> 00:01:17.726
Cole asked.

27
00:01:17.746 --> 00:01:21.529
"I think it would be cool to have a new ice-cream place in my neighborhood!"

28
00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.149
Emma shrugged.

29
00:01:23.169 --> 00:01:24.690
"I'm not sure.

30
00:01:25.711 --> 00:01:27.712
But I should go home too," she said.

31
00:01:28.564 --> 00:01:31.205
"I told my dad I'd help him give our dog a bath."

32
00:01:32.446 --> 00:01:34.066
She said good-bye and hurried away.

33
00:01:34.086 --> 00:01:38.008
"That was weird," Cole said when she was gone.

34
00:01:38.028 --> 00:01:41.450
"Robby seemed really angry when we mentioned Mr.

35
00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.150
Tate." "Yeah.

36
00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.492
He always seems pretty happy at school," Henry said.

37
00:01:46.512 --> 00:01:49.633
"Maybe he should be our first suspect."

38
00:01:51.074 --> 00:01:52.714
"Do you think Robby stole Mr.

39
00:01:52.754 --> 00:01:53.615
Tate's ice cream?"

40
00:01:53.915 --> 00:01:54.595
Maggie asked.

41
00:01:54.615 --> 00:01:56.356
"Why would he do that?"

42
00:01:57.572 --> 00:02:01.774
"All those kids were acting weird just now, not just Robby," Henry said.

43
00:02:01.794 --> 00:02:03.955
"Any of them could have done it."

44
00:02:04.975 --> 00:02:06.136
Maggie looked doubtful.

45
00:02:06.156 --> 00:02:11.298
"You think one of those kids broke into the Dessert Den and carried off all Mr.

46
00:02:11.318 --> 00:02:12.198
Tate's ice cream?"

47
00:02:12.218 --> 00:02:14.579
"Maybe they didn't carry it off."

48
00:02:14.899 --> 00:02:15.540
Cole grinned.

49
00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.480
"Maybe they ate it!"

50
00:02:18.301 --> 00:02:22.342
"Mr. Tate didn't say his ice cream was stolen," Henry reminded them.

51
00:02:22.362 --> 00:02:26.084
"He said his ice-cream flavor was stolen."

52
00:02:27.432 --> 00:02:28.452
"What does that mean?"

53
00:02:28.792 --> 00:02:29.833
Maggie looked confused.

54
00:02:30.513 --> 00:02:32.173
"How can someone steal a flavor?"

55
00:02:32.193 --> 00:02:34.834
"I don't know," Henry said.

56
00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.695
"Let's ask Mr.

57
00:02:36.735 --> 00:02:37.655
Tate when we see him.

58
00:02:38.555 --> 00:02:40.836
We need to find out exactly what happened."

59
00:02:43.136 --> 00:02:45.677
They walked their bikes the rest of the way to the Dessert Den.

60
00:02:46.517 --> 00:02:49.398
As they got closer, Henry saw a plumber leaving the shop.

61
00:02:54.059 --> 00:02:55.960
Cole said, peering inside the front door.

62
00:02:56.916 --> 00:02:58.217
"This place looks cool!"

63
00:02:59.098 --> 00:02:59.818
Henry nodded.

64
00:03:00.559 --> 00:03:04.261
The Dessert Den had big glass windows and a fancy sign out front.

65
00:03:05.242 --> 00:03:10.786
Inside, tables and chairs were painted in bright colors, and there were bins filled with candy and other

66
00:03:10.826 --> 00:03:15.569
treats. The front door was locked, but Henry could see Mr.

67
00:03:15.589 --> 00:03:16.310
Tate inside.

68
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.252
He was sweeping the floor in the dining area.

69
00:03:20.012 --> 00:03:21.093
Maggie knocked on the door.

70
00:03:22.014 --> 00:03:24.756
Mr. Tate looked up and then came over to unlock the door.

71
00:03:27.672 --> 00:03:29.033
"Hello," he greeted them.

72
00:03:29.774 --> 00:03:31.995
He sounded a lot more cheerful than he had earlier.

73
00:03:32.015 --> 00:03:33.536
"You're just in time."

74
00:03:34.897 --> 00:03:35.878
"Just in time for what?"

75
00:03:36.118 --> 00:03:38.340
Cole asked as he walked inside with the others.

76
00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.281
"Did you solve the mystery?"

77
00:03:41.242 --> 00:03:42.262
"No, nothing like that."

78
00:03:43.103 --> 00:03:45.965
Mr. Tate hurried over to the shiny, tiled counter.

79
00:03:46.946 --> 00:03:48.687
Several white boxes were sitting there.

80
00:03:48.707 --> 00:03:54.251
"I just got a very special delivery—some of the caramel-swirl brownies I'll be selling.

81
00:03:55.031 --> 00:03:55.612
Want a taste?"

82
00:03:56.996 --> 00:03:58.517
"Sure!" Cole said eagerly.

83
00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:00.378
"I love brownies!"

84
00:04:00.398 --> 00:04:04.199
"You love every kind of dessert," Maggie reminded him.

85
00:04:05.199 --> 00:04:06.220
Mr. Tate chuckled.

86
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.541
"Great! You're my perfect customer."

87
00:04:10.982 --> 00:04:13.943
He opened one of the boxes and handed each of the kids a brownie.

88
00:04:15.224 --> 00:04:16.264
Henry tasted his.

89
00:04:16.284 --> 00:04:19.925
"Yum! This is delicious!"

90
00:04:20.206 --> 00:04:20.666
he said.

91
00:04:21.326 --> 00:04:22.546
Cole and Maggie agreed.

92
00:04:22.566 --> 00:04:24.927
"I'm glad you like it," Mr.

93
00:04:24.947 --> 00:04:26.068
Tate said, smiling.

94
00:04:26.988 --> 00:04:29.689
"Tell all your friends to come to my grand opening tomorrow, okay?"

95
00:04:29.709 --> 00:04:32.671
"Sure." Cole licked his fingers.

96
00:04:32.691 --> 00:04:36.532
"But first, maybe you should tell us more about your mystery."

97
00:04:37.453 --> 00:04:38.953
Mr. Tate's smile faded.

98
00:04:39.654 --> 00:04:42.175
He glanced at a menu that was hanging above the counter.

99
00:04:43.135 --> 00:04:44.976
Henry could only see part of the menu.

100
00:04:45.656 --> 00:04:46.997
The rest was covered with a sheet.

101
00:04:47.017 --> 00:04:52.079
"You said someone stole your new ice-cream flavor," Henry reminded him.

102
00:04:52.099 --> 00:04:54.220
"What does that mean?"

103
00:04:55.712 --> 00:04:58.834
"The Dessert Den is going to serve all kinds of desserts," Mr.

104
00:04:58.854 --> 00:04:59.395
Tate said.

105
00:04:59.415 --> 00:05:01.976
"But one of our specialties is ice cream.

106
00:05:02.917 --> 00:05:06.159
So I invented a brand-new, exclusive flavor for my grand opening.

107
00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.521
It's supposed to be top secret.

108
00:05:09.281 --> 00:05:12.724
But somehow, someone found out about it—and stole it!"

109
00:05:13.785 --> 00:05:15.646
"How does someone steal a flavor?"

110
00:05:15.926 --> 00:05:16.666
Maggie wondered.

111
00:05:16.687 --> 00:05:19.989
"And who would do something like that, anyway?"

112
00:05:20.289 --> 00:05:20.949
Cole added.

113
00:05:20.969 --> 00:05:23.491
"I know exactly who stole it!"

114
00:05:23.551 --> 00:05:24.412
Mr. Tate snapped.

115
00:05:25.332 --> 00:05:27.074
"I just need you kids to help me prove it!"

116
00:05:28.096 --> 00:05:29.938
Henry felt more confused than ever.

117
00:05:30.839 --> 00:05:33.562
"You already know who stole your flavor?"

118
00:05:33.823 --> 00:05:34.263
he said.

119
00:05:34.283 --> 00:05:36.706
"Who?" Mr.

120
00:05:36.746 --> 00:05:37.647
Tate scowled.

121
00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:39.249
"It was Mrs.

122
00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.012
Sweet, who owns the Sweet Shop!"
